I'll analyze this candidate by examining the crypto module structure and understanding the security implications of importing PyCrypto functions. Let me start by exploring the file structure and related crypto modules.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "list_files",
  "arguments": {
    "pattern": "beaker/crypto/*.py"
  },
  "reason": "Explore the crypto module structure to understand what implementations are available"
}

Now let me examine the PyCrypto implementation to understand what functions are being imported and their security characteristics.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "read_file",
  "arguments": {
    "path": "beaker/crypto/pycrypto.py"
  },
  "reason": "Examine the PyCrypto implementation to understand the imported functions' behavior"
}

Let me also check the JCE crypto implementation to understand the alternative being used.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "read_file",
  "arguments": {
    "path": "beaker/crypto/jcecrypto.py"
  },
  "reason": "Examine the JCE crypto implementation to compare with PyCrypto"
}

Now let me check how these crypto functions are used in the main code to understand the security context.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "search_code",
  "arguments": {
    "query": "aesEncrypt",
    "path": "beaker",
    "max_results": 10
  },
  "reason": "Find where aesEncrypt is used to understand the security context and data flow"
}

Let me examine the session.py file to see how the crypto functions are actually used.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "file_context",
  "arguments": {
    "path": "beaker/session.py",
    "line": 430,
    "radius": 10
  },
  "reason": "Examine how aesEncrypt is used in session handling to understand the security context"
}

Let me see more of the decrypt function to understand the complete flow.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "file_context",
  "arguments": {
    "path": "beaker/session.py",
    "line": 440,
    "radius": 10
  },
  "reason": "See the complete decrypt flow to understand how aesDecrypt is used"
}

Now let me check how the crypto module is imported and used in session.py to understand the complete context.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "search_code",
  "arguments": {
    "query": "import crypto",
    "path": "beaker/session.py",
    "max_results": 5
  },
  "reason": "Find how the crypto module is imported in session.py"
}

Let me also check the PBKDF2 implementation to understand the key generation.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "read_file",
  "arguments": {
    "path": "beaker/crypto/pbkdf2.py",
    "start_line": 1,
    "end_line": 50
  },
  "reason": "Examine PBKDF2 implementation to understand key generation security"
}
